<h1>
<font color="#000000">Internet Speculative Fiction DataBase</font></h1></center>

<hr>
<center><font color="#000000"><b>Updated:</b> DBASEDATE</font>
<hr></center>

<p><font color="#000000"><font size=+3>Searches
</font></font><font size=+0>can
be performed by author, title, series, or year. Award lists can be directly
generated by year, as well as a yearly fiction index and forthcoming books.
Author bibliographies contain hot links to collaborators, award listings,
and publication data. Authors listed in the award listings or publication
content lists are hotlinks to specific author bibliographies.</font>
<table BORDER=0 CELLPADDING=5 >
<tr ALIGN=LEFT>
<td><a href="http://HTMLBASE/award.html">AWARDS</a></td>

<td>Generate an award listing for a specific award and year.</td>
</tr>

<tr ALIGN=LEFT>
<td><a href="http://HTMLBASE/entry.html">DATA ENTRY</a></td>

<td>Use this page to enter new authors or magazines into the database.</td>
</tr>

<tr ALIGN=LEFT>
<td><a href="http://HTMLBASE/stats4.html">DIRECTORY</a></td>

<td>All of the authors present in the ISFDB are listed in the author directory.</td>
</tr>

<tr ALIGN=LEFT>
<td><a href="http://HTMLBASE/derived.html">DERIVED</a></td>

<td>A page of pages pointing to interesting tidbits derived from the database,
such as the Top 100 lists, most-reviewed books, oldest living authors,
and the age graphs.</td>
</tr>

<tr ALIGN=LEFT>
<td><a href="http://DBASELOC/forthcoming.cgi">FORTHCOMING</a></td>

<td>List of known forthcoming books.</td>
</tr>

<tr ALIGN=LEFT>
<td><a href="http://HTMLBASE/zines.html">MAGAZINES</a></td>

<td>Display the contents of selected SF magazines.</td>
</tr>

<tr ALIGN=LEFT>
<td><a href="http://HTMLBASE/search.html">SEARCH</a></td>

<td>Search the DataBase by title, author, year, or series name - or generate
a fiction index for a particular year.</td>
</tr>

<tr ALIGN=LEFT>
<td><a href="http://HTMLBASE/printseries.html">SERIES</a></td>

<td>A collection of pages devoted to cataloging print series, such as Ace
Doubles, Ace Specials, Tor Doubles, etc...</td>
</tr>
</table>

